I reviewed the KML symbol anchoring and sizing logic and found two issues in the KML parser:

1. The “origin” in readVec2() is inverted – fraction/pixel units in KML are measured from the top‐left, not the bottom‐left, so the computed IconOrigin was wrong.  
2. Custom (non‐default) KML icons never got the default scale multiplier (DEFAULT_IMAGE_SCALE_MULTIPLIER) applied, so they render full‐size instead of half‐size by default.

Below are two *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches in `src/ol/format/KML.js` to correct both problems.  

